      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your high-density racking in Rotterdam, a proper understanding of the center of gravity (CG) is crucial; it's best to keep the load's CG as low as possible, ideally near the base of the stack. When stacking heavy industrial loads, you want to minimize overhangs and ensure the load is distributed evenly across the pallet footprint. Think of a pyramid structure, even if it's just two layers—a wide, stable base prevents the whole thing from toppling over, which is the most critical aspect of stacking stability. Always consult the racking manufacturer's load charts for specific weight limits per bay.",
